            <ArticleTitle>Microwave-assisted routes for rapid and efficient modification of layered perovskites.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7dt03865h</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Recent advances in exploiting microwave radiation in the topochemical modification of layered oxide perovskites are presented. Such methods work well for rapid bulk synthetic steps used in the production of novel inorganic-organic hybrids (protonation, grafting, intercalation, and in situ click reactions), exfoliation to produce dispersed nanosheets, and post-exfoliation processing to rapidly vary nanosheet surface groups. Compared to traditional methods that often take days, microwave methods can produce quality products in as little as 1-2 h.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
